# Line endings.
#
# Every text file in this tree is LF, in git and in the working copy. That was
# true by accident until now, which let a tooling slip rewrite 13 files as CRLF
# and turn a 179-line change into an 11,788-line one. This file makes it a rule.
#
# eol=lf rather than plain text=auto: the working copy gets LF on Windows too.
# That is already the state on disk, so this introduces no churn, and MSVC, rc.exe
# and PowerShell all read LF without complaint.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Images must never be touched. text=auto guesses correctly on these today, but a
# guess is not a guarantee and a single normalised byte corrupts them.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
